\title{datalib: access the UNICEF survey-microdata library from R}
\description{
Resolves, lists and loads survey microdata held in a \strong{datalib library} -- a
folder tree whose names encode the survey, its version and its provenance, so
the library needs no database and no index. \code{datalib} is the R port of the
language-neutral \strong{datalib contract v1}, shared byte-for-byte with the Stata
and Python implementations.
}
\section{The grammar, in one line}{
\preformatted{<root>/<CCC>/<CCC>_<YYYY>_<SURVEY>/<vintage>/<section>/}

A \strong{vintage} is either a \emph{master} (\verb{_vNN_M}) or an \emph{adaptation}
(\verb{_vNN_M_vNN_A_<COLLECTION>}). An adaptation names the master it derives from,
which is what lets \code{\link[=datalib_resolve]{datalib_resolve()}} answer "the HLT adaptation of the latest
master" from the folder names alone. \strong{Sections} are \code{Data/Stata},
\code{Data/Original}, \code{Data/R}, \code{Data/Other}, \code{Doc} and \code{Programs}.

\preformatted{Z:/datalib/ZWE/ZWE_2019_MICS/ZWE_2019_MICS_v02_M_v01_A_HLT/Data/Stata/
                                           |    |    |   |   |   |
                                   country_|    |    |   |   |   |_ collection
                                       year_____|    |   |   |
                                         survey______|   |   |_ adaptation v01
                                             master v02______|}
}

